ort points.","claim_ref":"sha256:9a43c3eddb32c8ae6201629ef2e4df2d94167dc286a45dd429a8dff192df88b5/nodes/support.contact"},{"claim_id":"support.contact_derivatives","kinds":["derivation"],"rationale":"Derives interior contact slopes and treats the one-sided origin condition separately from an interior minimum.","claim_ref":"sha256:9a43c3eddb32c8ae6201629ef2e4df2d94167dc286a45dd429a8dff192df88b5/nodes/support.contact_derivatives"}],"query_href":"/api/v1/papers/query?manifest=41f03ec0a8b1d30d68310120008da72a73f8c3f4cc88d65acbde651f5ad06a20&paper=long&passage=contact&representation=matches","reading_href":"/api/v1/papers/reading?manifest=41f03ec0a8b1d30d68310120008da72a73f8c3f4cc88d65acbde651f5ad06a20&paper=long&passage=contact"},{"ref":"sha256:267b41919f95376c728c2f90f5c80e4bf7aa13ca3418d4931ff608c908902e54/papers/short.md/sha256:cfbe950801fd334d8fd957243fa3b1f716ef609148c5f2ff97d44f9a6443d82c/papers/short.json/passages/contact","stage":"short","anchor":"contact","content_span":{"start_byte":9141,"end_byte":12026,"start_line":181,"end_line":243},"section_ref":"sha256:267b41919f95376c728c2f90f5c80e4bf7aa13ca3418d4931ff608c908902e54/papers/short.md/sections/9060","section_title":"2. Minimality gives contact; curvature excludes gaps","claim_refs":["sha256:9a43c3eddb32c8ae6201629ef2e4df2d94167dc286a45dd429a8dff192df88b5/nodes/support.contact","sha256:9a43c3eddb32c8ae6201629ef2e4df2d94167dc286a45dd429a8dff192df88b5/nodes/support.contact_derivatives","sha256:9a43c3eddb32c8ae6201629ef2e4df2d94167dc286a45dd429a8dff192df88b5/nodes/support.first_variation"],"evidence_class":"source_argument","treatments":[{"claim_id":"support.contact","kinds":["derivation"],"rationale":"Derives nonnegative tail cost and its vanishing on the support by feasible atom addition and compact fractional mass removal. The first-variation formula and regularity are cited inputs, and the sign conclusion uses minimality.","claim_ref":"sha256:9a43c3eddb32c8ae6201629ef2e4df2d94167dc286a45dd429a8dff192df88b5/nodes/support.contact"},{"claim_id":"support.contact_derivatives","kinds":["derivation"],"rationale":"Derives the value and slope conditions from derivatives of the contact function, with a separate right-hand expansion at zero. The origin argument retains contact at zero when zero belongs to the support and the zero-field identity q(0)=0.","claim_ref":"sha256:9a43c3eddb32c8ae6201629ef2e4df2d94167dc286a45dd429a8dff192df88b5/nodes/support.contact_derivatives"}],"query_href":"/api/v1/papers/query?manifest=41f03ec0a8b1d30d68310120008da72a73f8c3f4cc88d65acbde651f5ad06a20&paper=short&passage=contact&representation=matches","reading_href":"/api/v1/papers/reading?manifest=41f03ec0a8b1d30d68310120008da72a73f8c3f4cc88d65acbde651f5ad06a20&paper=short&passage=contact"},{"ref":"sha256:93145ef5687bb57439b6b2cb17b3f040069f7144f8a92e8bed7d3d18237af961/papers/expository.md/sha256:479155de953858e60f1454491ccda2215d88a4c2780e686cdfb8422481c62d9c/papers/expository.json/passages/first-variation","stage":"expository","anchor":"first-variation","content_span":{"start_byte":25223,"end_byte":26865,"start_line":590,"end_line":625},"section_ref":"sha256:93145ef5687bb57439b6b2cb17b3f040069f7144f8a92e8bed7d3d18237af961/papers/expository.md/sections/104","section_title":"Why the SK order parameter has no gaps","claim_refs":["sha256:9a43c3eddb32c8ae6201629ef2e4df2d94167dc286a45dd429a8dff192df88b5/nodes/support.first_variation"],"evidence_class":"source_argument","treatments":[{"claim_id":"support.first_variation","kinds":["statement","explanation"],"rationale":"States the admissible one-sided derivative formula and explains the separate penalty and reoptimised-control contributions. Nonnegativity of the derivative requires a minimiser; the cited formula itself applies to admissible coefficients and feasible directions.","claim_ref":"sha256:9a43c3eddb32c8ae6201629ef2e4df2d94167dc286a45dd429a8dff192df88b5/nodes/support.first_variation"}],"query_href":"/api/v1/papers/query?manifest=41f03ec0a8b1d30d68310120008da72a73f8c3f4cc88d65acbde651f5ad06a20&paper=expository&passage=first-variation&representation=matches","reading_href":"/api/v1/papers/reading?manifest=41f03ec0a8b1d30d68310120008da72a73f8c3f4cc88d65acbde651f5ad06a20&paper=expository&passage=first-variation"},{"ref":"sha256:93145ef5687bb57439b6b2cb17b3f040069f7144f8a92e8bed7d3d18237af961/papers/expository.md/sha256:479155de953858e60f1454491ccda2215d88a4c2780e686cdfb8422481c62d9c/papers/expository.json/passages/zero-candidate","stage":"expository","anchor":"zero-candidate","content_span":{"start_byte":45248,"end_byte":46415,"start_line":1070,"end_line":1108},"section_ref":"sha256:93145ef5687bb57439b6b2cb17b3f040069f7144f8a92e8bed7d3d18237af961/papers/expository.md/sections/44775","section_title":"7. Optional calculations","claim_refs":["sha256:9a43c3eddb32c8ae6201629ef2e4df2d94167dc286a45dd429a8dff192df88b5/nodes/support.diffusion","sha256:9a43c3eddb32c8ae6201629ef2e4df2d94167dc286a45dd429a8dff192df88b5/nodes/support.first_variation","sha256:9a43c3eddb32c8ae6201629ef2e4df2d94167dc286a45dd429a8dff192df88b5/nodes/support.moment_identity","sha256:9a43c3eddb32c8ae6201629ef2e4df2d94167dc286a45dd429a8dff192df88b5/nodes/support.regularity","sha256:9a43c3eddb32c8ae6201629ef2e4df2d94167dc286a45dd429a8dff192df88b5/nodes/support.zero_candidate_descent"],"evidence_class":"example","treatments":[{"claim_id":"support.first_variation","kinds":["application"],"rationale":"Applies the derivative formula to gamma=0 and the feasible constant direction, obtaining a negative cost and hence a nonminimising example. The calculation does not apply a minimiser-only contact or saturation conclusion.","claim_ref":"sha256:9a43c3eddb32c8ae6201629ef2e4df2d94167dc286a45dd429a8dff192df88b5/nodes/support.first_variation"},{"claim_id":"support.moment_identity","kinds":["application"],"rationale":"Uses the general moment identity with the explicit heat curvature to calculate q0 prime and q0. The displayed value q0(1/2)=1/3 distinguishes that general identity from the minimiser-only identity q=t.","claim_ref":"sha256:9a43c3eddb32c8ae6201629ef2e4df2d94167dc286a45dd429a8dff192df88b5/nodes/support.moment_identity"}],"query_href":"/api/v1/papers/query?manifest=41f03ec0a8b1d30d68310120008da72a73f8c3f4cc88d65acbde651f5ad06a20&paper=expository&passage=zero-candidate&representation=matches","reading_href":"/api/v1/papers/reading?manifest=41f03ec0a8b1d30d68310120008da72a73f8c3f4cc88d65acbde651f5ad06a20&paper=expository&passage=zero-candidate"}],"semantic_certification":false,"coverage":{"query_truncated":false,"source_bytes_opened":false,"receipt_bytes_opened":false,"selection_policy":"query_papers whole-passage selection; union within each selector family, intersection between families","authored_link_policy":"Links incident to selected passages, in their stored direction; target_stage filters the other endpoint","shared_claim_policy":"Exact claim_ids intersection only; other stages by default, or the explicitly selected target stage","treatment_policy":"Only explicit authored treatments are returned; a missing treatment is unspecified, including in legacy mappings","ordering":"Cards and sources follow stage then document byte order; links follow annotation basis, endpoints, kind and identity; no importance ranking","scope":"Reading guidance and passage correspondence only. Shared claims assert neither equivalence nor complete explanation. Authored derivation, application or illustration treatments do not establish a proof, prerequisite edge, discharged hypothesis or accepted evidence. Further consequences, alternative routes and formal transport obligations retain their recorded scope."},"items":[{"from_anchor":"zero-candidate","from_text_sha256":"4b77dc2bc524cb1964d0563fa2c157d68830278f95852be5b3f4bd6e75668db5","to_stage":"expository","to_anchor":"first-variation","to_text_sha256":"1599517ba173cb1d62338b2c2479d3ba003873c0377af094605128d210d5a709","kind":"illustrates","rationale":"Uses the zero coefficient and